WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.530
More than 250 million people live in a country
other than the one they were born in... in

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.120
other words, they’re immigrants.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:16.530
And, my friends, this number won’t stop
growing.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.961
In the last 50 years it has multiplied by
3 and only since the year 2000, the number

00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:23.750
of immigrants has increased by 80 million!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:35.460
That’s 80 million more people who’ve left
their country in search of a better life.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.850
And as you can imagine, most of all the world’s
immigrants – more than 65% - have settled

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:51.309
in the richest countries, such as the United
States, Germany, Australia and Canada.

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:54.420
And it is precisely this fact, dear viewers
of VISUALPOLITIK, that is feeding, throughout

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.450
the world...

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:00.670
controversial, furious and bitter debates
on immigration.... and also, the discourse

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:03.059
of many populist movements.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:09.070
In recent years, in Europe, for example, we’ve
seen a lot of populist and xenophobic parties

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:17.810
emerging... which have targeted immigration
directly.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.579
What if they steal our jobs, put us in danger,
destroy our national identity, etc., etc.

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:28.479
But... perhaps, the most outstanding case
is that of Donald Trump.

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:33.170
A president who has made it clear, very clear,
that he really doesn’t like immigration...

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.909
except, apparently, under certain circumstances.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.369
Check it out:

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:41.279
("President Trump balked at an immigration
deal that would include protections for people

00:01:41.279 --> 00:01:44.659
from Haiti and some nations in Africa, demanding
to know

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:50.929
why he should accept immigrants from “s***hole
countries” rather than from places like

00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:51.929
Norway".

00:01:51.929 --> 00:01:52.929
New York Times)

00:01:52.929 --> 00:01:56.469
Why on earth would Trump think that Norwegians
want to emigrate en masse to the United States,

00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:58.789
when they are already richer than Americans?

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:03.700
In fact, more people are moving from the US
to Norway than the other way around.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.489
But... let's not stray off topic.

00:02:08.489 --> 00:02:13.739
Is immigration really a danger, a burden,
a step down?

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:20.410
Is the United States losing economic momentum
because of all the immigrants in the country?

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:27.819
Should the US stop the arrival of more foreigners?

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:35.629
Let's see.

00:02:35.629 --> 00:02:41.040
If there’s one thing we can all agree on,
it’s that we live in an increasingly interconnected

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.760
world, that is, a world where it’s becoming
easier, faster and cheaper to go from one

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.599
place to another.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:54.769
And where it’s also becoming easier to contact
our loved ones no matter where we are.

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:59.349
And... as you can imagine all these things
make the decision to pack up and move to another

00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:01.450
country much, much easier.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.200
That's why... if there were 90 million immigrants
around the world in the 60s, today there are

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:13.019
more than 250 million...

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:14.019
And you know what?

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:18.040
We can expect this number to grow strongly
in the upcoming years.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.459
First, because it’s becoming easier to move,
and second because of the huge demographic

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:25.249
growth that many poor countries are experiencing.

00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:31.319
So, my friends, the question is, are there
reasons to worry?

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:38.209
Listen up.

00:03:38.209 --> 00:03:48.040
(A LUCKY BREAK?)

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.660
Whenever rich countries talk about immigration,
it sounds like they’re debating whether

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.659
or not to engage in some kind of charity.

00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:56.239
And... you know what?

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:59.209
Nothing could be further from the truth.

00:03:59.209 --> 00:04:03.959
Immigration favors economic growth, among
other things because most immigrants are adults

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:05.099
of working age.

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:09.849
Therefore, it’s calculated, listen up, that
since the year 2000, immigrants have been

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:16.100
responsible for 40 to 80 percent of their
main recipient countries’ workforce growth.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:22.620
So let’s be honest without them, these countries
would be far less wealthy.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.099
But yes I know.

00:04:24.099 --> 00:04:28.790
This is all quite abstract, if you want we
can see exactly what has happened in one of

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:33.270
the countries where immigration has caused
a lot of controversy recently: the United

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:36.310
Kingdom.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:41.060
In recent years, while some political groups
warned about the enormous threat that immigration

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:43.780
- including, check this out, immigrants coming
from other European Union countries - posed

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.250
to British jobs, identity, and way of life...
the truth is that the economy has placed very,

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:54.870
very different numbers on the table.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.800
Never before in history, have so many people
been employed in the United Kingdom as they

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:05.020
have today-- neither in absolute nor relative
terms.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:15.410
And, it doesn’t even matter if we exclude
immigrants.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:20.830
Never before has the British population had
so many job opportunities as they do now.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:26.050
And…. not only that, according to studies
from several British universities...

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:31.099
all these immigrants pay more taxes than they
get from the State and if that weren’t enough,

00:05:31.099 --> 00:05:39.560
the UK is managing to attract more university
immigrants than any other European country.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:44.210
In other words: the effect of this immigration
is very, very positive for the British...

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:48.699
and it’s also helping turn the United Kingdom
into a technological powerhouse.

00:05:48.699 --> 00:05:49.699
Not bad, right?

00:05:49.699 --> 00:05:50.699
Well...

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:51.699
You know what?

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:52.960
Despite Trump's fiery speeches...

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.630
The truth is that on the other side of the
Atlantic, things really aren’t that different.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:02.630
Listen up.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:11.430
(THE NORTH AMERICAN DREAM)

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:16.460
With just over 44 million people – more
or less the population of Spain – the United

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:24.419
States is in absolute terms, the country with
the most immigrants in the world…

00:06:24.419 --> 00:06:29.960
However, just a moment... because in relative
terms...

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.389
things are different.

00:06:31.389 --> 00:06:36.599
These 44 million people, represent just under
14% of the entire population.

00:06:36.599 --> 00:06:41.340
To give you an idea, in countries like Australia
or New Zealand, for example, the percentage

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:45.390
is almost twice as high.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:54.560
Now, here’s a question and you can’t look
it up:

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.509
What impact do you think immigrants have in
the United States?

00:06:58.509 --> 00:07:00.199
Well dear viewers...

00:07:00.199 --> 00:07:01.889
listen up:

00:07:01.889 --> 00:07:05.919
Despite representing just under 14% of the
population, immigrants are responsible for

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:12.599
almost 25% of all businesses that open in
the United States; for more than 30% of the

00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:17.900
companies in which venture capital funds invest
and almost half of all of Silicon Valley’s

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.900
high-tech start-ups.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:25.970
And that's not all… according to a study
from the Center for American Entrepreneurship,

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:31.690
43% of the 500 largest companies in the United
States were founded either by immigrants or

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:37.720
by children of immigrants.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:54.139
That’s 216 companies whose revenues surpass
$5 trillion each year and employ almost 13

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:57.189
million people around the world.

00:07:57.189 --> 00:08:02.660
We’re talking about nearly half of the great
US economic powerhouse.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:07.610
My friends, from Henry Ford to Elon Musk...
many of the great figures and iconic characters

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:18.879
of the United States weren’t even born in
this country.

00:08:18.879 --> 00:08:19.889
But, just a moment...

00:08:19.889 --> 00:08:24.960
some of you may be thinking, OK, SIMON, but
those are only a few immigrants, the most

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.310
educated ones...

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.599
What about the rest?

00:08:28.599 --> 00:08:34.020
Well... the truth is, the numbers don’t
vary much there either: their entrepreneurship

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.810
and employment rates are also very high.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.260
And they provide several other benefits, too.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:42.640
For example, in a country that at the moment,
let's not forget, has pretty much full employment,

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:47.630
new immigrants reinforce the US’s competitiveness,
encourage the rest of the American population

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.670
to do more, and allow for many businesses
that would’ve otherwise not existed to be

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.140
created.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:09:00.890
So in summary: immigrants reduce the population’s
average age, they have more children, are

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:04.010
more educated, are more enterprising, file
more patents, etc., etc.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:08.640
And if you think about it for a second, it
all makes a lot of sense:

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:13.070
on the one hand, these people arrive to achieve
a better future, so they are willing to take

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.260
risks and work hard;

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:19.660
on the other hand, they have had different
experiences and education, and they can take

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:22.320
advantage of this to progress.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.220
Think, for example, of the Italian pizzas
or the Mexican tacos that flood the US today...

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.890
and the rest of the world.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:33.100
Well, despite these arguments… and of the
fact that never before have so many Americans

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:37.270
had jobs, politicians like Donald Trump still
don’t like immigration.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:38.590
But you know what?

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:46.540
This isn’t the first time that US political
leaders have spoken out against immigration.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:53.960
(THE PRECEDENTS)

00:09:53.960 --> 00:10:04.850
My friends, this is by no means the first
time that the United States, the country of

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.680
immigrants, has had political campaigns against
immigration.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:12.400
See, in the middle of the 19th century, the
political movement "Know Nothing" opposed

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:17.420
immigrants, particularly the Irish.... and
soon after, the Chinese had their turn.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.770
Yes, you heard that right...

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.520
the Chinese!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:25.320
During the second half of the nineteenth century,
many Chinese came to the United States...

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:29.190
and that triggered a rather hostile popular
reaction.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:34.260
( From Seattle to Los Angeles, from Wyoming
to the small towns of California, immigrants

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:40.010
from China were forced out of business, run
out of town, beaten, tortured, lynched, and

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:43.360
massacred, usually with little hope of help
from the law.”

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.370
Immigration, a work of Library Of Congress.)

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:51.960
All this because, at that time, Americans
saw the Chinese as competition.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:57.230
And in 1882 the Federal Congress itself approved
the Law of Exclusion of the Chinese, which

00:10:57.230 --> 00:11:02.030
not only suspended the arrival of new Chinese
immigrants but, also, made the lives of those

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:06.560
who were already in the US quite complicated.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:07.980
And that wasn’t all.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:12.170
In 1924, after around 30 million people had
crossed the Atlantic Ocean to reach the US,

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:16.380
Washington established a quota policy that
greatly reduced the number of immigrants that

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:19.910
could arrive and also... vetoed immigrants
from southern Europe – such as Spain and

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:22.380
Italy –, Eastern Europe, Asia and Africa.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:25.370
So basically, the few who could enter had
to be Anglo-Saxons.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:35.490
And, more recently, in 1994, the then governor
of California, Pete Wilson, blamed Hispanic

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.770
immigrants for the state’s poor economic
situation… and

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.630
Do you know what he did?

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:44.620
Well... he launched a huge political campaign
against immigration and pushed the so-called

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:50.820
Proposition 187, a law that prevented access
to social, educational and even health services

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.170
for all irregular immigrants.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.210
Including children!

00:11:55.210 --> 00:12:03.480
It was so aggressive that just a year later
the supreme court declared it unconstitutional.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:13.990
Well, the fact is that despite all these campaigns
against immigration...

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:18.860
existing research shows that states and counties
that historically had more immigration, now

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:23.670
have a higher income, less poverty, less unemployment
and better educational results.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:27.420
So with all this data in mind, it might be
good for both the White House and the Capitol

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:31.510
to focus less on how to deport people and
more on how to strengthen access,

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:36.600
and to try to approve, once and for all, a
migratory reform that facilitates the orderly

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:41.930
arrival of more people... more workers, more
entrepreneurs and more researchers to aid

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.120
the great North American economy.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.990
By the way, in a future video, which we’ll
try to make available very soon on our PATREON

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:54.120
page and later here on this Channel, we’ll
discuss each of the great myths about immigration.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.120
But now, it’s your turn.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.330
Do you think your country should reduce the
entry of immigrants?

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:03.371
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

00:13:03.371 --> 00:13:07.180
I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did and don’t forget to

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.080
subscribe to our channel for brand new videos.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:12.740
Also, don’t forget to check out our friends
at the Reconsider Media Podcast - they provided

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.760
the vocals in this episode that were not mine!

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:24.860
And as always, thanks for watching!

